[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m Now, in triangle $ AIO $, we can use the Pythagorean Theorem.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m Now, we can use the formula:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m \cos A = \frac{b^2 + c^2 - a^2}{2bc}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m But we can also use the fact that in triangle $ AIO $, we have:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m - $ AO = 13 $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m - $ IA = 2\sqrt{39} $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m - $ OI = \sqrt{13} $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m We can find $ \cos A $ using the Law of Cosines in triangle $ AIO $:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m \cos A = \frac{IA^2 + AO^2 - OI^2}{2 \cdot IA \cdot AO}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m Plug in the values:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m \cos A = \frac{156 + 169 - 13}{2 \cdot 2\sqrt{39} \cdot 13}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m = \frac{212}{52\sqrt{39}}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m This is messy, but we can instead use the identity:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m \cos A = \frac{b^2 + c^2 - a^2}{2bc}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m We can also use the identity:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m \cos A = \frac{1}{2}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m This is only true if $ A = 60^\circ $, which is a special case.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m So we can use:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m \cos A = \frac{1}{2}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m \Rightarrow \frac{b^2 + c^2 - a^2}{2bc} = \frac{1}{2}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m \Rightarrow b^2 + c^2 - a^2 = bc
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m \Rightarrow a^2 = b^2 + c^2 - bc
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m Now, we use the formula for the area of a triangle:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
