[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m ### Step 1: Understand the notation
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m In base $ b $, the number $ 17_b $ means:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 17_b = 1 \cdot b + 7 = b + 7
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m Similarly, $ 97_b = 9 \cdot b + 7 = 9b + 7 $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m We are told that $ 17_b $ divides $ 97_b $, i.e.,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 9b + 7 \equiv 0 \pmod{b + 7}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m ### Step 2: Use modular arithmetic
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m We want:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 9b + 7 \equiv 0 \pmod{b + 7}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m This means that:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 9b + 7 = k(b + 7) \quad \text{for some integer } k
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m Let’s simplify the expression $ 9b + 7 $ modulo $ b + 7 $.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m Divide $ 9b + 7 $ by $ b + 7 $:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 9b + 7 = 9(b + 7) - 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 9b + 7 \equiv -56 \pmod{b + 7}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m But we want:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 9b + 7 \equiv 0 \pmod{b + 7}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m -56 \equiv 0 \pmod{b + 7}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m \Rightarrow b + 7 \mid 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m ### Step 3: Find all divisors of 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m We now find all positive integer divisors of 56, and subtract 7 from each (since $ b + 7 \mid 56 \Rightarrow b = d - 7 $, where $ d $ is a divisor of 56 and $ b > 9 $).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m First, find the divisors of 56:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 56 = 2^3 \cdot 7^1
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m The positive divisors of 56 are:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 1, 2, 4, 7, 8, 14, 28, 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m Now subtract 7 from each to get possible values of $ b $:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m - $ d = 1 \Rightarrow b = 1 - 7 = -6 $ (invalid)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m - $ d = 2 \Rightarrow b = 2 - 7 = -5 $ (invalid)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m - $ d = 4 \Rightarrow b = 4 - 7 = -3 $ (invalid)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m - $ d = 7 \Rightarrow b = 7 - 7 = 0 $ (invalid)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m - $ d = 8 \Rightarrow b = 8 - 7 = 1 $ (invalid)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m - $ d = 14 \Rightarrow b = 14 - 7 = 7 $ (invalid, since $ b > 9 $)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m - $ d = 28 \Rightarrow b = 28 - 7 = 21 $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m - $ d = 56 \Rightarrow b = 56 - 7 = 49 $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m So the valid values of $ b $ are:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
