[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m ### Step 2: Use modular arithmetic
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m We want to find when $ b + 7 $ divides $ 9b + 7 $. That is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 9b + 7 \equiv 0 \pmod{b + 7}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m We can simplify the expression:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 9b + 7 \equiv 0 \pmod{b + 7}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m \Rightarrow 9b + 7 \equiv 0 \pmod{b + 7}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m Let’s write this as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 9b + 7 = k(b + 7) \quad \text{for some integer } k
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m Now, solve for $ k $:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 9b + 7 = k(b + 7)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m \Rightarrow 9b + 7 = kb + 7k
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m \Rightarrow 9b - kb = 7k - 7
