[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m ### Step 1: Understand the Geometry
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m - A **rhombus** has **equal diagonals** that intersect at the **center** (the origin in this case).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m - The diagonals of a rhombus bisect each other at right angles.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m - In a rhombus, the diagonals are perpendicular and bisect each other.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m - So, if the diagonals intersect at the origin, then the **diagonals are along the x-axis and y-axis**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m Let the diagonals be:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m - $AC$ along the x-axis: from $(-a, 0)$ to $(a, 0)$, so the length is $2a$
