[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m This implies that the incenter $ I $ lies on a line perpendicular to $ \overline{OI} $ at point $ A $, i.e., the vector $ \vec{IA} $ is perpendicular to $ \vec{OI} $.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m This is a special configuration, and often in such problems, it's helpful to use coordinate geometry or vector geometry.
