[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m ### Step 1: Convert times to hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m - 4 hours = 4 hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m - 2 hours and 24 minutes = 2 + $ \frac{24}{60} = 2.4 $ hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m ### Step 2: Use the distance = speed × time formula
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m Let’s denote:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m - $ d = 9 $ km (distance)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m - $ s $ = speed in km/h
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m - $ t $ = time in minutes spent in the coffee shop
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m ### Step 3: First scenario: $ s $ km/h
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m She walks 9 km at speed $ s $, takes 4 hours, including $ t $ minutes.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m Convert total time to hours:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m \text{Total time in hours} = 4 \text{ hours}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
