[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m ### Step 2: Use known formulas
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m We can use the following known formulas:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m - The **distance between the incenter and circumcenter** is given by:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m   $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m   OI^2 = R^2 - 2Rr
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m   $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m   (This is a known formula from triangle geometry.)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m Let’s compute $ OI^2 $:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m OI^2 = R^2 - 2Rr = 13^2 - 2 \cdot 13 \cdot 6 = 169 - 156 = 13
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m \Rightarrow OI = \sqrt{13}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
