[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m ### Step 3: Use the fact that $ IA \perp OI $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m This means that $ IA $ is a **perpendicular** to $ OI $, so the triangle $ OIA $ is a **right triangle** with right angle at $ I $.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m So, we can apply the **Pythagorean Theorem** in triangle $ OIA $:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m OI^2 + IA^2 = OA^2
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m We know $ OI = \sqrt{13} $, and $ OA = R = 13 $, so:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m (\sqrt{13})^2 + IA^2 = 13^2 \Rightarrow 13 + IA^2 = 169 \Rightarrow IA^2 = 156
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m \Rightarrow IA = \sqrt{156} = 2\sqrt{39}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m $$
