[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m ### Step 3: Use the Rhombus Property
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m In a rhombus, the diagonals are **perpendicular**. So the vectors $ \vec{AC} $ and $ \vec{BD} $ are perpendicular.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=13765)[0m Let’s compute the slopes of the diagonals:
